\section{Style configuration}{

A key must be configured before it can be used in a mark. New
documents know these keys: \code{bold}, \code{italic}, and \code{underline} (which
expand \code{"after"}), and \code{link}, \code{highlight}, \code{comment}, and \code{code}
(which expand \code{"none"}).

The expand behavior decides whether text inserted at a boundary of a
marked range joins the mark: \code{"after"} for text inserted at its end,
\code{"before"} at its start, \code{"both"}, or \code{"none"}.

Each call to \code{doc_config_text_style()} sets the complete
configuration: the built-in keys, overridden or extended by the keys
given in \code{...}. The configuration is local to a replica and is not
synchronized, so every replica should configure a key the same way.
}

